From: Uke Linux maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mfd: qcom-spmi-pmic: check the optional Uke PM8010 population

The selected Uke firmware can retain the generic PM8010 N node without
advertising a PM8010 in SMEM or any of its N regulator resources in the
command DB. Admit that exact optional node before a transport read. Other
boards, nodes and populated variants keep their ordinary probe path.
Missing or malformed firmware evidence is an error, never an absence result.

The project-owned helper is installed alongside this source by preparation.
No generic transport error, revision value or PMIC power state is changed.

--- a/drivers/mfd/qcom-spmi-pmic.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/qcom-spmi-pmic.c
@@ -17,6 +17,8 @@
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
 #include <soc/qcom/qcom-spmi-pmic.h>
 
+#include "uke-pm8010.h"
+
 #define PMIC_REV2		0x101
 #define PMIC_REV3		0x102
 #define PMIC_REV4		0x103
@@ -252,6 +254,13 @@ static int pmic_spmi_probe(struct spmi_device *sdev)
 	struct qcom_spmi_dev *ctx;
 	int ret;
 
+	ret = uke_pm8010_should_probe(sdev);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return dev_err_probe(&sdev->dev, ret,
+				     "Cannot verify optional Uke PM8010 population\n");
+	if (!ret)
+		return -ENODEV;
+
 	regmap = devm_regmap_init_spmi_ext(sdev, &spmi_regmap_config);
 	if (IS_ERR(regmap))
 		return PTR_ERR(regmap);
